      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastopol%2C_California",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sebastopol’s roots lie in plum and apple orchards, a heritage that still echoes in its annual Apple Blossom Festival and Gravenstein Apple Fair.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastopol%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The $32‑million Barlow Mall turned old agricultural warehouses into a marketplace for dining, tasting rooms, and art, cementing Sebastopol’s place in Wine Country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastopol%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "During the COVID‑19 pandemic, the former Sebastopol Inn was transformed into Elderberry Commons, a supportive housing community funded by Project Homekey.",
